lockdown orders and fear of the  coronavirus caused economic activity to  plunge  and unemployment to skyrocket at an  unprecedented rate  the first task of the next president  will be to deal with the economic  destruction  that the pandemic has brought the  president should not confuse economic  growth for economic strength  the economy will continue to recover  rapidly throughout the second half of  2020  with double-digit gdp growth but these  growth rates are relative to the second  quarter of 2020 when gdp plunged to the  32  annual rate why does this matter because  it's important to recognize that despite  exploding economic growth  the economy is still very weak and these  eye-popping projections are more an  indication of past economic weakness  than current economic strength they  reflect a fast  climb out of a very deep hole and there  is much more climbing left to do  the economy will still need fiscal  support to avoid a slow and sluggish  recovery  and to prevent short-term economic  damage from causing  deeper problems that will hurt the  economy for years to come  what policies do you think the next  president should pursue to support the  economy  let us know in our poll and let us know  what other topics you'd like our  scholars to cover in 60 seconds  and be sure to like and subscribe for  more research and videos  from aei
 

